WEBVTT

00:00:04.090 --> 00:00:08.500
Mobile Suit Zeta Gundam

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:15.580
ima wa ugokenai sore ga sadame dakedo

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:15.580
Right now I can't move... That is my fate, but...

00:00:15.630 --> 00:00:20.720
akirame wa shinai mou mezameta kara

00:00:15.630 --> 00:00:20.720
I won't give up anymore because I have awakened.

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:25.890
moeru tokimeki wa jidai wo utsushi

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:25.890
My burning, throbbing heart reflects the era...

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:31.060
iro azayaka ni moesakaru honoo

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:31.060
It has the color of vividly blazing flames...

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:35.820
Crying ima wa mienaku tomo

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:35.820
Crying, though I can't see it right now...

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:40.350
Searching michi shirube wa ukabu

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:40.350
Searching, a guidepost floats up ahead.

00:00:40.350 --> 00:00:43.170
I wanna have a pure time!

00:00:43.170 --> 00:00:48.280
Everyone's a noble mind!

00:00:48.330 --> 00:00:53.500
soko ni nokotta wakasa toridashi

00:00:48.330 --> 00:00:53.500
I'll take out what remains of my youth there,

00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:55.980
Believing a sign of Zeta,

00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:00.540
beyond the hard times from now!

00:01:01.290 --> 00:01:06.320
kawaku kuchibiru nureteiru nara

00:01:01.290 --> 00:01:06.320
If these dry lips become wet,

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:11.460
toki wo norikoe atsui jidai e to

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:11.460
Beyond time, towards a passionate era,

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:16.500
utsuru darou to shinjiteiru kara

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:16.500
Because I believe it will move...

00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:19.060
Believing a sign of Zeta,

00:01:19.060 --> 00:01:23.690
beyond the hard times from now...

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:35.850
Entering the Atmosphere

00:02:07.830 --> 00:02:11.260
Are you telling me to turn this ship,
the Hario, toward Earth's orbit?!

00:02:11.330 --> 00:02:15.030
If you want me to defeat the A.E.U.G.,
you should.

00:02:19.870 --> 00:02:23.310
If you have no intention of doing so, I'm
returning to the mother ship Jupitris.

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:26.810
We have no definite information
that the A.E.U.G. gathering at Side 4...

00:02:26.880 --> 00:02:29.480
...will be headed for Earth.

00:02:29.550 --> 00:02:32.180
Well, what good are we if we just stay here?

00:02:33.690 --> 00:02:35.480
I'll get in touch with Captain Bask!

00:02:35.560 --> 00:02:37.920
I ask that you stay in this ship for now.

00:02:37.990 --> 00:02:39.120
Very well.

00:02:39.190 --> 00:02:42.190
Seems I've forgotten how to get by
in the secular world.

00:02:42.260 --> 00:02:43.890
I'll oversee the reloading of the Messala
as I wait.

00:02:44.600 --> 00:02:45.570
I'd appreciate that.

00:02:45.630 --> 00:02:47.830
- Only for two hours, though.
- Y-Yes!

00:02:50.370 --> 00:02:53.240
Why did the Captain select some guy
like that, just returning from Jupiter?

00:03:15.960 --> 00:03:17.760
Check C-armor parts!

00:03:17.830 --> 00:03:19.890
Checking C-armor parts... no problems.

00:03:19.970 --> 00:03:20.630
Okay, Kamille!

00:03:21.500 --> 00:03:23.300
Lunch is here!

00:03:24.740 --> 00:03:26.470
Kamille, go grab your lunch.

00:03:26.540 --> 00:03:27.730
Huh? But we're still...!

00:03:27.810 --> 00:03:28.800
Hurry!

00:03:37.020 --> 00:03:39.140
Enjoy your lunch.

00:03:39.220 --> 00:03:41.120
What are you doing that for?

00:03:41.190 --> 00:03:42.490
I have no time to be fooling around.

00:03:42.990 --> 00:03:46.020
Everyone's so busy around here,
so I should help in any way that I can.

00:03:46.290 --> 00:03:49.320
- Is that wrong?
- If it's an order, it can't be helped.

00:03:49.400 --> 00:03:51.990
Mr. Astonaige!
There aren't enough.

00:03:52.670 --> 00:03:54.160
Amuro! You're not well!

00:03:54.240 --> 00:03:56.170
It's Kamille!

00:03:59.810 --> 00:04:01.210
Captain Bright.

00:04:01.280 --> 00:04:04.470
The timing on take-off is a lot different
from that of the White Base.

00:04:04.550 --> 00:04:05.880
Yes, I can tell.

00:04:05.950 --> 00:04:08.420
Hi, Kamille. Where's Lieutenant Quattro?

00:04:08.420 --> 00:04:10.350
Sir! He's by the Hyaku Shiki!

00:04:12.320 --> 00:04:13.340
<i>Lieutenant Quattro!</i>

00:04:13.420 --> 00:04:16.690
<i>Let me introduce you to our newly</i>
<i>appointed captain! Come over here!</i>

00:04:19.660 --> 00:04:22.390
As of today, he's to be addressed
as Captain Bright.

00:04:22.460 --> 00:04:24.160
Well, that's great news.

00:04:24.230 --> 00:04:27.690
- I expect I'll be counting on you.
- My pleasure.

00:04:27.770 --> 00:04:29.930
I'm thrilled to be able to see your skills
first hand.

00:04:30.370 --> 00:04:33.100
But my senses aren't quite as keen
as they were.

00:04:33.170 --> 00:04:35.330
If anyone, you'll do just fine,
Captain Bright.

00:04:36.710 --> 00:04:38.740
I'm also counting on you, Kamille Bidan!

00:04:38.810 --> 00:04:39.510
Bright!

00:04:40.010 --> 00:04:41.310
How are you?

00:04:42.020 --> 00:04:44.040
Haro? How come?

00:04:44.490 --> 00:04:46.320
I found it on Amman.

00:04:46.390 --> 00:04:48.180
It could be the Haro from back then.

00:04:48.260 --> 00:04:49.650
No.

00:04:49.720 --> 00:04:51.660
Even the toy versions were
programmed with...

00:04:51.730 --> 00:04:54.320
...the names of Amuro and Bright.

00:04:54.400 --> 00:04:55.990
Now, Captain Bright!

00:05:00.470 --> 00:05:02.130
- Bye.
- No, Kamille.

00:05:02.200 --> 00:05:04.670
You are to have this special meal package
for the pilots!

00:05:05.570 --> 00:05:07.440
Never mind. Just give me
what everyone else is having!

00:05:07.510 --> 00:05:09.810
It's part of the military rules!
You must abide by them!

00:05:10.940 --> 00:05:12.570
All right, then! Bye.

00:05:12.850 --> 00:05:15.040
Hey, do you know the situation
with Captain Bright?

00:05:15.620 --> 00:05:16.580
Huh?

00:05:16.750 --> 00:05:19.380
I hear his wife and children live on Earth.

00:05:20.090 --> 00:05:23.390
What's he going to do
now that he's joined the A.E.U.G.?

00:05:23.460 --> 00:05:24.580
I don't know!

00:05:24.660 --> 00:05:28.890
The Earth Federation Government
may take his family hostage!

00:05:28.960 --> 00:05:31.160
- We don't know that!
- What are you all upset about?!

00:05:34.070 --> 00:05:35.800
Stop showing off!

00:05:35.870 --> 00:05:37.000
Bright, where are you?!

00:05:37.240 --> 00:05:38.830
Amuro, where are you?

00:05:38.910 --> 00:05:40.170
Haro, stop it!

00:05:47.480 --> 00:05:51.420
Can this ship encounter the A.E.U.G.'s fleet
before they enter the atmosphere?

00:05:51.650 --> 00:05:54.880
Sure it can. We could block them
on their way in.

00:05:54.960 --> 00:05:58.080
I'm glad to return to Earth,
but are you confident we can pull this off?

00:05:58.460 --> 00:06:00.950
We've both trained extensively
on the simulation.

00:06:01.030 --> 00:06:02.790
And the Marasai's been performing well
as of late.

00:06:02.860 --> 00:06:05.230
Yes, we may even be able to pay them
back for what happened on the Moon.

00:06:06.100 --> 00:06:08.530
- To the Gundam Mk. II, right?
- Right!

00:06:08.600 --> 00:06:10.700
I never dreamed I'd be able to return
to Earth so soon.

00:06:12.110 --> 00:06:14.010
I'll go help with the adjustments
on the ballutes.

00:06:14.070 --> 00:06:15.770
Got a lover waiting or something?

00:06:15.840 --> 00:06:17.240
Anything wrong with that?

00:06:33.330 --> 00:06:33.850
Okay.

00:06:33.930 --> 00:06:36.290
Lieutenant Emma's good eyesight helps.

00:06:36.360 --> 00:06:37.760
I'm beginning to get a feel for things.

00:06:37.830 --> 00:06:39.920
- You catch on quickly.
- Thank you.

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:43.830
I hear your family's in Jaburo.
Are you okay with this?

00:06:44.370 --> 00:06:45.960
I'm not worried.

00:06:46.040 --> 00:06:48.370
She's practically a Newtype herself.

00:06:48.440 --> 00:06:50.470
Please tell me more about your wife.

00:06:50.540 --> 00:06:52.140
Her name is Mirai Yashima.

00:06:52.210 --> 00:06:55.150
She was the White Base's steersperson
during the One Year War.

00:06:55.220 --> 00:06:56.150
Is that so?!

00:06:56.220 --> 00:06:58.810
- Then he's got nothing to worry about.
- I'm convinced.

00:06:58.890 --> 00:07:01.910
And I've talked to her about
taking a position with the A.E.U.G..

00:07:01.990 --> 00:07:05.120
It's all yours from this point on. I'm returning
to the Moon on that transport ship.

00:07:05.190 --> 00:07:06.660
Yes, sir!

00:07:07.930 --> 00:07:10.090
- You don't have to see me off.
- Yes, sir!

00:07:11.400 --> 00:07:13.490
- How many children?
- Two.

00:07:13.570 --> 00:07:16.160
A boy and a girl?

00:07:16.240 --> 00:07:18.000
How did you know?

00:07:20.110 --> 00:07:21.700
A lucky guess.

00:07:34.560 --> 00:07:36.680
You're late.

00:07:36.760 --> 00:07:38.750
I'm sorry. What is it, sir?

00:07:38.830 --> 00:07:42.190
Well, it's disappointing to have to part with
such a skilled subordinate like yourself...

00:07:42.260 --> 00:07:44.760
- ...but...
- Yes?

00:07:45.400 --> 00:07:49.230
I need you to lead the unit
that will storm into Jaburo.

00:07:55.380 --> 00:07:56.710
Good luck...!

00:07:56.780 --> 00:07:58.750
- Ah!
- What are you doing in a place like this?!

00:07:58.980 --> 00:08:00.910
I got lost.

00:08:04.790 --> 00:08:07.580
This is a very busy time. Goodbye!

00:08:08.820 --> 00:08:10.950
You mustn't come into places like this!

00:08:11.460 --> 00:08:13.430
Yes, ma'am.

00:08:13.590 --> 00:08:15.590
Did you have a fight
with Kamille or something?

00:08:15.660 --> 00:08:16.190
No.

00:08:17.930 --> 00:08:19.020
Hey!

00:08:23.240 --> 00:08:26.500
Kamille's been under a lot of stress
so he's acting like a spoiled brat...

00:08:26.570 --> 00:08:28.200
...at the sight of a familiar face.
That's why...!

00:08:28.280 --> 00:08:31.300
I understand the feelings of a pilot!

00:08:31.380 --> 00:08:33.870
Please leave me alone!

00:08:42.020 --> 00:08:44.080
Don't send out our mobile suits?

00:08:44.160 --> 00:08:46.560
That's what I said.
Didn't you hear me the first time?!

00:08:47.360 --> 00:08:48.690
But why?!

00:08:48.760 --> 00:08:50.860
If my Messala can do the job on its own...

00:08:50.930 --> 00:08:52.870
...we have no reason to use
these outdated models!

00:08:52.930 --> 00:08:54.630
Bastard!

00:08:55.440 --> 00:08:58.560
I understand these would be different from
mobile suits you use around Jupiter, but...!

00:08:58.970 --> 00:09:02.430
The Messala is a trial model I helped
manufacture while on Jupitris.

00:09:02.510 --> 00:09:05.970
The only reason I pursued the Temptation
with it was to see how it would perform.

00:09:06.680 --> 00:09:07.700
It's a trial model?

00:09:08.080 --> 00:09:09.410
Just watch and see.

00:09:18.230 --> 00:09:21.960
All vessels! Proceed with caution
for obstacles in our path!

00:09:22.030 --> 00:09:25.230
- All sensors cleared automatic check!
- Course clear!

00:09:25.970 --> 00:09:27.660
Proceed in Earth's direction!

00:09:46.620 --> 00:09:48.110
I'm using the ballute, Kacricon!

00:09:48.960 --> 00:09:52.520
- <i>Can you hear me?!</i>
- Yeah, I'm watching. Go ahead!

00:09:52.860 --> 00:09:56.160
<i>Here I go! Three, two, one...!</i>

00:09:58.800 --> 00:10:01.290
Okay, the size is just right!

00:10:01.370 --> 00:10:04.460
This'll allow us to enter the atmosphere
with no problems.

00:10:06.810 --> 00:10:10.300
<i>Hurry up and attach the ballute capsules</i>
<i>to the units!</i>

00:10:11.210 --> 00:10:13.270
The rest is a matter of guts.

00:10:17.920 --> 00:10:19.480
Okay, Kamille! Looks good!

00:10:19.950 --> 00:10:23.290
- Was the timing okay?!
- Everything's fine!

00:10:24.120 --> 00:10:27.390
Can this hover really support
the Gundam's weight?

00:10:27.460 --> 00:10:28.950
According to calculations, yes.

00:10:29.760 --> 00:10:30.490
What do you mean?

00:10:31.160 --> 00:10:33.960
If you stick your hand outside of the flying
armor during entry into the atmosphere...

00:10:34.030 --> 00:10:36.630
...even the Gundam
will easily lose a hand.

00:10:36.700 --> 00:10:38.530
- I'm aware of that.
- Okay!

00:10:38.610 --> 00:10:41.370
- Get some rest until we begin operations!
- Bye!

00:10:42.280 --> 00:10:44.970
I understand you clearly.
I wish you the best of luck.

00:10:45.050 --> 00:10:46.810
Now, get some rest
until we commence operations.

00:10:47.350 --> 00:10:49.040
Later.

00:10:49.120 --> 00:10:51.310
- Lieutenant Quattro.
- Yes?

00:10:51.390 --> 00:10:53.350
I have a request.

00:10:54.320 --> 00:10:55.310
About your family?

00:10:57.190 --> 00:10:59.220
If by chance they're still in Jaburo...!

00:11:00.290 --> 00:11:02.760
I'll see what I can do about rescuing them.

00:11:02.830 --> 00:11:04.920
Where in Jaburo is your family situated?

00:11:05.000 --> 00:11:06.300
Shall I draw you a map?

00:11:06.370 --> 00:11:07.860
That'll help.

00:11:18.180 --> 00:11:20.240
I hear that your parents died.

00:11:20.310 --> 00:11:22.750
You don't have to try
to look surprised, you know!

00:11:22.820 --> 00:11:23.710
Kamille!

00:11:23.780 --> 00:11:25.750
I knew nothing about it.

00:11:26.150 --> 00:11:30.820
I honestly feel bad about it, that even your
parents are suspected because of me...

00:11:30.890 --> 00:11:33.720
...and you had to flee as a result!

00:11:34.330 --> 00:11:35.390
However!

00:11:35.660 --> 00:11:38.290
It can't be helped!
I can't do anything about it!

00:11:38.370 --> 00:11:40.560
I'm not doing what I am
because I want to, you know!

00:11:41.000 --> 00:11:43.230
But...!

00:11:43.300 --> 00:11:45.070
But I-I don't know what I should do either.

00:11:45.140 --> 00:11:48.340
Sure, I'd like to comfort you, but...!

00:11:48.410 --> 00:11:51.310
I'm also still a child!

00:11:51.380 --> 00:11:52.470
Take it easy on me!

00:11:52.550 --> 00:11:55.380
Well, so am I!
So just leave me alone, will you?!

00:11:55.450 --> 00:11:57.350
Damn you!

00:12:15.200 --> 00:12:16.600
Let's do it!

00:12:23.140 --> 00:12:25.110
Secure orbit! Secure fleet position!

00:12:25.350 --> 00:12:27.780
Mobile suit launch holders of all vessels,
secured!

00:12:28.120 --> 00:12:30.880
Ready for take off! Be extra cautious
for enemies from all surrounding areas!

00:12:31.250 --> 00:12:32.220
Roger!

00:12:34.620 --> 00:12:36.560
Lieutenant Quattro, good luck!

00:12:36.620 --> 00:12:38.960
- <i>Roger, Captain!</i>
- Thanks.

00:12:40.230 --> 00:12:41.090
I'm going!

00:12:41.160 --> 00:12:43.390
Gundam Mk. II, ready for take-off!

00:12:43.460 --> 00:12:45.190
Rick Dias, ready for take-off!

00:12:51.870 --> 00:12:53.840
Kamille, you're leaving, are you?

00:12:54.070 --> 00:12:55.770
Gundam, launching!

00:13:31.380 --> 00:13:33.310
Attacking Jaburo, are you?

00:13:33.380 --> 00:13:36.110
That's understandable, but I won't allow it!

00:13:41.050 --> 00:13:42.020
Okay.

00:13:56.170 --> 00:13:57.160
The Sicilia's been destroyed!

00:13:57.340 --> 00:13:59.100
What?! Where were you watching?!

00:13:59.310 --> 00:14:02.370
Mobile suit on portside!
No, it's a mobile armor!

00:14:02.440 --> 00:14:03.470
- What kind?
- What kind?!

00:14:03.880 --> 00:14:05.850
Umm... Checking data.

00:14:06.750 --> 00:14:07.580
Type, unknown!

00:14:12.920 --> 00:14:14.280
The formation is off.

00:14:14.820 --> 00:14:16.220
<i>Jibyan and Sul behind us...!</i>

00:14:16.290 --> 00:14:18.150
They've been hit?! By the Titans?!

00:14:20.160 --> 00:14:22.090
Miss Emma! Are you breaking the formation?!

00:14:22.630 --> 00:14:24.930
Emma's unit moved away?!
Tell her to stop!

00:14:25.000 --> 00:14:26.860
Have Kamille go instead,
Lieutenant Quattro!

00:14:26.930 --> 00:14:27.870
<i>Roger!</i>

00:14:27.930 --> 00:14:29.490
Emma's unit is key to the formation.

00:14:31.270 --> 00:14:33.570
The flying armor has greater mobility!

00:14:33.640 --> 00:14:35.610
It's crucial that we have Emma's unit
descend to Jaburo!

00:14:35.980 --> 00:14:36.770
Right!

00:14:36.840 --> 00:14:39.110
The Hyaku Shiki must remain
until the formation is complete.

00:14:39.180 --> 00:14:40.440
- Go!
- Yes, sir!

00:14:43.020 --> 00:14:44.280
Fall, little pest!

00:14:48.420 --> 00:14:51.320
Lieutenant Emma! You're to lead
the mobile suit troops in front!

00:14:51.390 --> 00:14:54.220
Don't stop sending out mobile suits
from the respective vessels!

00:14:54.290 --> 00:14:55.350
Lieutenant Emma!

00:14:55.430 --> 00:14:57.450
Make them hurry with their entrance
into the atmosphere!

00:14:57.860 --> 00:15:00.920
Machine gun platform! Put up a barrage
without hitting our own units!

00:15:01.170 --> 00:15:02.400
You guys are taking forever!

00:15:06.810 --> 00:15:09.780
I never knew the Titans had developed
such a mobile armor.

00:15:10.340 --> 00:15:14.580
The purpose of that organization isn't just
to track down remnants of the Zabi Clan.

00:15:18.050 --> 00:15:19.350
Two units at once?!

00:15:19.420 --> 00:15:20.580
<i>Miss Emma! Watch out!</i>

00:15:20.650 --> 00:15:22.320
That's the guy from the other day!

00:15:23.020 --> 00:15:24.250
There's no way she's hearing me!

00:15:32.070 --> 00:15:33.590
Lieutenant! I'm telling you he's dangerous!

00:15:33.900 --> 00:15:35.160
Who's that?

00:15:37.740 --> 00:15:38.930
Is that the one from...?

00:15:40.370 --> 00:15:43.040
I've arranged to have Apolly and Roberto's
Rick Dias units lead the formation.

00:15:43.110 --> 00:15:45.040
I'm heading over to assist Emma's unit!

00:15:45.110 --> 00:15:46.240
Roger!

00:15:46.310 --> 00:15:49.440
- Destroy that unidentified mobile armor!
- Roger!

00:15:49.680 --> 00:15:51.670
However, I imagine this opponent
isn't just any old enemy.

00:15:59.590 --> 00:16:00.520
It transformed!

00:16:05.670 --> 00:16:06.290
Fall!

00:16:10.370 --> 00:16:12.000
I told you!

00:16:14.910 --> 00:16:16.100
Kamille! Keep your distance!

00:16:16.810 --> 00:16:18.780
Is that the one called the Gundam Mk. II?

00:16:23.820 --> 00:16:25.750
You're only a minor change!

00:16:28.220 --> 00:16:29.750
He avoided it! With that?!

00:16:35.260 --> 00:16:37.560
Lieutenant Emma! Forget about Kamille!

00:16:37.630 --> 00:16:38.390
Retreat!

00:16:40.400 --> 00:16:41.420
But...!

00:16:41.500 --> 00:16:43.560
<i>Head back to the Argama!</i>

00:16:46.310 --> 00:16:48.070
<i>It's undoubtedly different!</i>

00:16:48.140 --> 00:16:50.040
<i>He's not Amuro!</i>

00:16:50.110 --> 00:16:51.670
<i>He's a different type!</i>

00:16:52.380 --> 00:16:54.710
No mistake about it! Starboard!
Forty degrees above!

00:16:54.780 --> 00:16:57.050
It's an enemy mobile suit troop!

00:16:57.120 --> 00:16:59.110
- You're sure, are you?!
- What'll we do, sir?!

00:16:59.490 --> 00:17:01.680
If they're coming from the front,
our troops should notice!

00:17:01.760 --> 00:17:05.280
If we can get two-thirds of our force
to Jaburo, we can take over the place!

00:17:05.360 --> 00:17:06.660
Try to get past this!

00:17:10.360 --> 00:17:12.850
Main artillery, can't you see?!
Get the barrage up!

00:17:12.930 --> 00:17:15.590
Mobile suit units! Descend below
the horizontal line of the fleet!

00:17:15.670 --> 00:17:17.500
Four minutes to atmospheric entry, sir!

00:17:18.410 --> 00:17:21.170
Ignore the enemy! Have everyone
focus on the mobile suit formation!

00:17:32.450 --> 00:17:35.650
- Is the Gundam Mk. II out there?
- <i>Take it easy! Think about where we are!</i>

00:17:36.120 --> 00:17:37.250
You'll find yourself pulled by the gravity!

00:17:37.320 --> 00:17:40.020
<i>That's exactly why</i>
<i>this is such a great chance!</i>

00:17:40.090 --> 00:17:40.960
You have a point.

00:17:45.370 --> 00:17:46.960
This pressure! What is it?!

00:17:53.570 --> 00:17:54.540
It's leaving!

00:17:59.080 --> 00:18:01.740
That mobile suit transformed.

00:18:02.650 --> 00:18:05.850
I'm not about to be pulled in
by Earth's gravity.

00:18:05.920 --> 00:18:07.410
I'll leave the rest to the reinforcements.

00:18:08.290 --> 00:18:10.260
We're going to the front of the fleet!

00:18:10.320 --> 00:18:11.850
The Titans have begun
with their second wave of attacks!

00:18:12.490 --> 00:18:13.460
Yes!

00:18:14.160 --> 00:18:15.960
Who is that guy?

00:18:21.270 --> 00:18:22.600
Hey, you! It's dangerous out there!

00:18:24.400 --> 00:18:26.030
Lieutenant Emma, please retreat!

00:18:26.340 --> 00:18:27.670
There's no way I can do that!

00:18:27.740 --> 00:18:29.440
I must descend to Jaburo!

00:18:33.480 --> 00:18:35.810
Is Kamille okay?

00:18:36.050 --> 00:18:38.020
What are you doing here?!
Return to your room!

00:18:38.080 --> 00:18:39.380
Right now, that wouldn't be safe.

00:18:39.450 --> 00:18:41.280
Have her sit over there.

00:18:41.350 --> 00:18:44.980
- One minute to atmospheric entry.
- Emma's unit has lost an arm, sir.

00:18:45.060 --> 00:18:45.820
What?!

00:18:45.890 --> 00:18:47.760
Stop her from entering the atmosphere!

00:18:47.830 --> 00:18:50.690
Lt. Emma, return at once! You can't enter
the atmosphere in your condition!

00:18:51.160 --> 00:18:51.990
<i>I'm okay.</i>

00:18:52.070 --> 00:18:54.300
<i>I'll have no problem</i>
<i>entering the atmosphere!</i>

00:18:54.370 --> 00:18:56.860
<i>These are captain's orders!</i>
<i>Lieutenant Emma! Retreat!</i>

00:19:00.540 --> 00:19:01.600
I see it!

00:19:02.710 --> 00:19:04.180
Here they come!

00:19:07.880 --> 00:19:10.780
We're entering the atmosphere!
Emma! Cut the crap!

00:19:13.920 --> 00:19:15.750
It's time! We're entering the atmosphere!

00:19:15.820 --> 00:19:18.260
We're retrieving Emma's unit!
Argama, descend!

00:19:32.110 --> 00:19:33.070
Lieutenant Quattro.

00:19:34.270 --> 00:19:36.270
Abide by Captain Bright's orders!

00:19:36.880 --> 00:19:37.600
Lieutenant Quattro!

00:19:38.040 --> 00:19:39.740
Begin atmospheric entry!

00:19:39.810 --> 00:19:42.870
The barrage isn't enough!
Our mobile suits will be shot down!

00:19:50.020 --> 00:19:51.790
This time...! This time for sure!

00:19:55.330 --> 00:19:58.350
Doesn't that new model realize
that we're losing altitude?!

00:19:58.430 --> 00:19:59.360
It'll burn up in flames!

00:19:59.770 --> 00:20:01.260
Lieutenant! I wish for your safety!

00:20:01.600 --> 00:20:03.540
- Protect the Argama for us!
- <i>Yes!</i>

00:20:05.640 --> 00:20:06.660
Reduce altitude!

00:20:06.740 --> 00:20:08.710
But it would be unsafe
to reduce altitude any further!

00:20:08.780 --> 00:20:09.740
Reduce it!

00:20:10.040 --> 00:20:12.030
There goes my chance.

00:20:14.680 --> 00:20:15.810
Contact made with Emma's unit!

00:20:15.880 --> 00:20:18.040
Increase altitude.
The fleet's getting out of here.

00:20:18.120 --> 00:20:19.110
Anti-air fire to rear!

00:20:19.190 --> 00:20:20.650
Commence our barrage!

00:20:20.720 --> 00:20:22.550
<i>Thank you very much!</i>

00:20:22.620 --> 00:20:24.090
<i>But I could've made it down to Earth!</i>

00:20:24.320 --> 00:20:25.290
What did you say?!

00:20:25.490 --> 00:20:27.980
Come to the bridge later!
I'll give you a "correction"!

00:20:28.930 --> 00:20:31.120
A mobile suit battle down on Earth
isn't a walk in the park...

00:20:31.200 --> 00:20:33.170
...as you might think, Lieutenant!

00:20:43.880 --> 00:20:44.840
Kamille!

00:20:45.110 --> 00:20:47.340
- What's the status with those behind us?
- They're following us, sir!

00:20:47.410 --> 00:20:48.280
And the enemy?!

00:20:48.350 --> 00:20:50.370
They appear to be descending to Earth
with our troops, sir!

00:20:55.660 --> 00:20:57.590
How long do you expect to last
without your ballute?!

00:21:01.730 --> 00:21:04.820
Against your Wave Rider,
I'm at a disadvantage with my ballute!

00:21:05.800 --> 00:21:07.030
How reckless!

00:21:09.000 --> 00:21:10.870
<i>Kacricon, you're not going to last</i>
<i>much longer!</i>

00:21:10.940 --> 00:21:12.700
But I'm finished if I open my ballute now!

00:21:13.540 --> 00:21:14.730
Guess we'll have to give it up!

00:21:17.080 --> 00:21:20.570
Jerid, you coward! We won't
defeat the enemy with that attitude!

00:21:23.080 --> 00:21:25.020
You're not going to last!
You'll burn to death!

00:21:30.190 --> 00:21:31.780
It's automatic!

00:21:34.530 --> 00:21:36.790
B-But at this rate, he'll get me!

00:21:37.660 --> 00:21:39.930
You would've survived
if you'd kept your distance!

00:21:54.380 --> 00:21:57.650
<i>Amelia!</i>

00:22:02.720 --> 00:22:03.690
Kacricon!!

00:22:05.930 --> 00:22:08.330
If I had gone ahead...!

00:22:10.100 --> 00:22:12.960
I'll get them for this.
I promise, Kacricon.

00:22:47.270 --> 00:22:49.600
Oh, I can't help believing you

00:22:50.480 --> 00:22:56.020
kanarazu aeru to ano hi kara shinjiteita

00:22:50.480 --> 00:22:56.020
I've believed we're sure to meet again ever since that day

00:22:56.070 --> 00:23:01.400
kitto yobiau kokoro ga areba

00:22:56.070 --> 00:23:01.400
If we have heart, we'll be called together again

00:23:01.450 --> 00:23:11.790
mugen no Energy yobisamasu

00:23:01.450 --> 00:23:11.790
Awaken the infinite energy

00:23:11.830 --> 00:23:17.420
aa kizutsukeau mae ni

00:23:11.830 --> 00:23:17.420
Before you get hurt

00:23:17.460 --> 00:23:23.510
dekiru koto sagashite Please

00:23:17.460 --> 00:23:23.510
Find what you can do...Please

00:23:23.550 --> 00:23:28.680
nagedasanai de kurushii toki koso

00:23:23.550 --> 00:23:28.680
Don't throw it away because of this painful age

00:23:29.390 --> 00:23:32.020
itsuka mita aoi sora wo

00:23:29.390 --> 00:23:32.020
Until the day we gaze up again

00:23:32.030 --> 00:23:39.030
kitto anata to miageru hi made

00:23:32.030 --> 00:23:39.030
at the blue sky we once saw

00:23:46.310 --> 00:23:48.400
Having successfully advanced to Jaburo...

00:23:48.470 --> 00:23:51.440
...Kamille and Char are able to rescue
Kai and Reccoa.

00:23:51.680 --> 00:23:55.140
However, there they find themselves
in a trap set by the Titans.

00:23:55.210 --> 00:23:56.270
Kamille trembles when he finds out...

00:23:56.350 --> 00:23:59.580
...about a tremendous ticking
nuclear bomb set to explode.

00:23:59.650 --> 00:24:02.450
Can the A.E.U.G. escape Jaburo?

00:24:03.190 --> 00:24:07.530
Next on Mobile Suit Zeta Gundam,
"The Winds of Jaburo".

00:24:07.470 --> 00:24:12.470
Next Episode

00:24:07.470 --> 00:24:12.470
The Winds of Jaburo

00:24:08.090 --> 00:24:10.830
You will see the tears of time.
